      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1330845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-19T14:54:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Come to think of it, I think this feels awkward because it belongs in the Makefile and board.mk.  I.e., that\u0027s normally where we do toolchain config, and also where we know about things like the architecutre so we can select the right compilers.",
      "parentUuid": "2c6c0dce_d1882d0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "256ed497530447085d921e89e6cdb8b5c5fedd86",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dff8454_190ebb67",
        "filename": "util/build_with_clang.py",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-09T18:28:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this case I wanted to avoid adding it to buildall. The Makefile is already complex, and I also don\u0027t want to force everyone to build the code twice (once with clang and once with gcc). This approach is similar to how zephyr has a separate build command. 99% of the time if it works with gcc it will work with clang, but we can still catch the 1% server-side.",
      "parentUuid": "0751fc8c_a6da8c75",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "256ed497530447085d921e89e6cdb8b5c5fedd86",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
